@.str.17 = private unnamed_addr constant [52 x i8] c"rewrite a path or closure to content-addressed form\00", align 1
@.str.18 = private unnamed_addr constant [2034 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Create a content-addressed representation of the closure of GNU Hello:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix store make-content-addressed nixpkgs#hello\0A  \E2\80\A6\0A  rewrote '/nix/store/v5sv61sszx301i0x6xysaqzla09nksnd-hello-2.10' to '/nix/store/5skmmcb9svys5lj3kbsrjg7vf2irid63-hello-2.10'\0A  ```\0A\0A  Since the resulting paths are content-addressed, they are always\0A  trusted and don't need signatures to copied to another store:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix copy --to /tmp/nix --trusted-public-keys '' /nix/store/5skmmcb9svys5lj3kbsrjg7vf2irid63-hello-2.10\0A  ```\0A\0A  By contrast, the original closure is input-addressed, so it does\0A  need signatures to be trusted:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix copy --to /tmp/nix --trusted-public-keys '' nixpkgs#hello\0A  cannot add path '/nix/store/zy9wbxwcygrwnh8n2w9qbbcr6zk87m26-libunistring-0.9.10' because it lacks a signature by a trusted key\0A  ```\0A\0A* Create a content-addressed representation of the current NixOS\0A  system closure:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix store make-content-addressed /run/current-system\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command converts the closure of the store paths specified by\0A[*installables*](./nix.md#installables) to content-addressed form.\0A\0ANix store paths are usually\0A*input-addressed*, meaning that the hash part of the store path is\0Acomputed from the contents of the derivation (i.e., the build-time\0Adependency graph). Input-addressed paths need to be signed by a\0Atrusted key if you want to import them into a store, because we need\0Ato trust that the contents of the path were actually built by the\0Aderivation.\0A\0ABy contrast, in a *content-addressed* path, the hash part is computed\0Afrom the contents of the path. This allows the contents of the path to\0Abe verified without any additional information such as\0Asignatures. This means that a command like\0A\0A```console\0A# nix store build /nix/store/5skmmcb9svys5lj3kbsrjg7vf2irid63-hello-2.10 \\\0A    --substituters https://my-cache.example.org\0A```\0A\0Awill succeed even if the binary cache `https://my-cache.example.org`\0Adoesn't present any signatures.\0A\0A\00", align 1
